        "committer": {
          "name": "Yonatan Nachum",
          "email": "ynachum@amazon.com",
          "date": "2026-05-30 19:06:01.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-20191 efalnd: Split conn cleanup into scan and drain stages",
        "message": "LU-20191 efalnd: Split conn cleanup into scan and drain stages\n\nSplit kefalnd_cleanup_ni_conns into two stages to reduce write lock\nhold time and improve cleanup responsiveness:\n\nStage 1 (kefalnd_scan_ni_conns, every 5s): Scan the hash table for\nidle or deactivating connections. Under read lock collect candidates\nonto a per-NI cleanup list. Under write lock re-validate and remove\nconfirmed idle connections from the hash table.\n\nStage 2 (kefalnd_drain_ni_conns, every 1s): Iterate the per-NI\ncleanup list without holding conn_lock. Drain abort and pending TXs\nand destroy fully drained connections. Early return when the list is\nempty so there is no cost in the common case.\n\nThis eliminates the fixed MAX_IDLE_CONN cap, moves TX cleanup out of\nthe write lock critical section, uses a consistent timestamp for TX\ntimeout checks, and ensures connections pending cleanup are also\ndestroyed on NI shutdown.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nChange-Id: I3c9aab473b71affc7863a4393e1cc99bde74f3e8\nSigned-off-by: Yonatan Nachum <ynachum@amazon.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
